;; GrimoNX809JCooling writes the fan control nodes, which the stock vendor policy labels
;; sysfs_nb_fan, under its own UID as platform_app. The stock system wrote them from
;; system_server instead, so two things the app needs were never there.
;;
;; init.nx809j.grimoireos.rc opens the nodes to 0666 at boot. That rc runs as init, and AOSP
;; lets init chmod only a short list of sysfs types; the setattr rule adds the fan nodes.
;;
;; The stock vendor policy already allows platform_app to write the nodes, but apps run at
;; their user's MLS level (s0:c512,c768 for the owner) and the nodes at s0, and the MLS
;; constraint lets a write cross levels only for a trusted subject or object. system_server
;; is a trusted subject. The stock vendor policy marks the pump's proc_ztelcd_set as a
;; trusted object, which is why the pump already works; this does the same for the fan.
;; Which domains may write the nodes is still up to the stock vendor policy's allow rules.
;;
;; The type is declared here because the build also compiles this file without the vendor
;; policy. The device compiles the policy with secilc -m, which accepts the repeated
;; declaration.

(type sysfs_nb_fan)
(allow init sysfs_nb_fan (file (setattr)))
(typeattributeset mlstrustedobject (sysfs_nb_fan))

;; GrimoNX809JAls joins the system UID and runs as system_app, the only client the stock vendor
;; policy allows for the subsys HAL it calls. It also reads the raw backlight level from
;; /sys/class/backlight/panel0-backlight/brightness, labelled vendor_sysfs_graphics. The stock
;; system read it from system_server; the stock vendor policy gives system_app search on the
;; directories and write, getattr and open on the files, but not read.

(type vendor_sysfs_graphics)
(allow system_app vendor_sysfs_graphics (file (read)))
